WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.767
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:02.767
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:03.567
We hope you're
doing well tonight

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.434
and now, if you don't mind,

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.501
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.901
President Biden published
an op-ed today

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:11.033
in The New York Times
and that man is spiraling.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.934
Fox News host Tucker Carlson
last night claimed

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.501
that the security camera footage
from the Capitol attack

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:22.534
"does not show an insurrection
or a riot in progress."

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.934
Yeah, okay,
but when you cherry-pick

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:27.400
the footage you're showing,
you can prove whatever you want.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.267
I could show you footage
from "John Wick"

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:31.400
that proves he's not violent.
Take a look.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.234
-[ Whining ]

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.868
-We'll grab you
some kibble later.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:39.501
[ Tender tune plays ]
[ Collar rings against bowl ]

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:42.234
-You're telling me that guy

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:43.501
[ Laughter ]
is a trained killer?

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:44.868
Give me a break!

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:45.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:47.667
The footage doesn't lie.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.434
After Fox News
host Tucker Carlson

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:52.434
aired exclusive security footage
from the Capitol attack,

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.634
former President Trump posted
on Truth Social,

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:57.467
"LET THE JANUARY 6
PRISONERS GO."

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.801
You guys know we can see
what you're doing, right?

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:03.200
[ Laughter ]
Kevin McCarthy,
who is Trump's Waylon Smithers,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.167
[ Laughter ]
gives all the footage
to Tucker;

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:07.167
Tucker shows
only the tame parts;

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.133
and then Trump claims
the rioters were framed.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.701
It's like watching a magic show

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:13.400
where the magician
is wearing sheer sleeves.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.701
They do have very nice sheer
sleeves on the magician.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.501
[ Laughter ]
Didn't know how
it was going to look.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.067
I find out with you guys.
It's the best way

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:24.167
to do quality control.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.968
In a new episode of her podcast,

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:29.000
former First Lady
Michelle Obama said

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.367
that she sobbed uncontrollably
for 30 minutes

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:32.501
after leaving the White House

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:33.968
at the end
of President Obama's term.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.767
As opposed to her husband,
who dealt

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.767
with his post-presidency grief
more stoically.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:41.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.801
Columbia University last week
announced they will no longer

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:48.200
require SAT or ACT scores
in undergraduate admissions,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.267
while UMass announced
that you no longer need

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.701
that show-and-tell project.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:59.067
Massachusetts' own
Mike Scollins.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.267
[ Laughter ]
In a new interview,

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.501
Transportation Secretary
Pete Buttigieg

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.834
pushed back against critics
characterizing him

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.367
as being elitist
and out of touch

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.400
and said his critics,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.234
"wouldn't know their way
around a T.J.Maxx

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.634
if their life depended on it."

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:16.033
[ Laughter ]
But if you're lost
inside a T.J.Maxx,

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:18.133
your life does depend on it.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:21.934
That's right,
Pete Buttigieg said,

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.968
"You think Tucker Carlson
knows the difference

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.667
between a T.J.Maxx
and a Kohl's?"

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:28.234
Actually, he might,
because aren't those his sons?

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.400
[ As Carlson ]
T.J.Maxx, Kohl!

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.434
It's time for lacrosse practice.
Let's go!

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:34.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:37.534
Grocery delivery service
Hello Fresh confirmed yesterday

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:39.801
it will stop selling
coconut milk from Thailand

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:42.300
over concerns
of forced monkey labor.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.400
From now on, they're only going
to use union monkeys.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.634
A group of entrepreneurs
in Massachusetts

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:53.934
have filed paperwork to open
a topless marijuana dispensary,

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:56.167
[ Oohs ]
though they might run
into some legal issues,

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.334
since they're ten.

00:02:57.334 --> 00:03:00.334
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.834
"Hi, we'd like to file
some papers.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:09.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:11.334
Yeah, we have an idea
for a business.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:14.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:17.100
Uh, can we -- can we put here
'Don't tell our parents'?"

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:20.968
And finally, in honor
of St. Patrick's Day,

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:23.901
Dairy Queen is offering its new
Under the Rainbow Shake,

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.601
which features
vanilla soft serve

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:26.801
and multicolored sprinkles.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.234
And Arby's is honoring
St. Paddy's Day

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:31.400
by driving all the snakes
out of the kitchen.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.834
[ Laughter ]
And that --

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:34.834
that was a monologue.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:35.834
We're off and running,
everybody.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:37.000
We got a great show
for you tonight.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.634
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:42.033
He is a dear,
dear friend of mine

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.834
with many credits --
"The Mindy Project,"

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:47.267
"Neighbors," "The Afterparty,"
but none of his credits make him

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:50.868
as happy as his new title
of Celebrity Jeopardy! Champion.

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.934
We'll talk about his
hilarious new show,

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:55.501
"History of the World, Part II,"
but probably not as much

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.334
as how he won all
of Celebrity Jeopardy!

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.601
The very funny Ike Barinholtz
is here tonight, everybody.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.667
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:06.400
She stars in "Scream VI,"
which is out this week.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.267
We'll be joined by the very
talented actress

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:09.634
Melissa Barrera.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:13.567
[ Cheering and applause ]
And she is the legendary author

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.801
of "The Handmaid's Tale"
and many others.

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.667
Her latest...

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:18.701
...is on sale now.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.300
The great Margaret Atwood

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.567
is back and joining us.

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:24.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
How exciting.

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:26.467
Before we get to all that,

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.133
if you've been following
the news recently,

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.601
you may have seen that movie
theater chain AMC plans

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:34.667
to start charging higher prices
for better seats in the theater.

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:36.701
You know, hearing things
like that always,

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:39.968
well, it gets me to thinking
I'm getting older, you guys,

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:43.167
[ Laughter ]
and sometimes
I don't even understand

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.934
the world I'm living in anymore.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.467
[ Southern accent ]
Things are changing every day,

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:50.367
and not always for the better.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:51.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:55.167
So, it's time to take a moment

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:59.667
to talk about how things were
just a little bit more simple

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:00.667
back in my day.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.300
[ Poignant tune plays ]

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.033
♪♪

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:11.901
Back in my day, AMC wasn't
charging more for better seats.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:14.400
Back in my day, if you wanted
good seats at the theater,

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.000
you could take your pick
because the year was 2021

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.367
and everyone else was afraid
to leave the house.

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:21.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:23.067
And if, by some miracle,

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:25.133
there was someone else
in the theater that day

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.834
and they were sitting
where you wanted to sit,

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:29.767
all you had to do was plop down
in the seat right next to them

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:30.968
and give a little cough.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:32.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.901
Right within striking distance
of their popcorn.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.133
Just a little one, like this.
[ Coughs ]

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.868
Pretty soon,
the whole place was yours.

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:41.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:43.834
Back in my day,
they weren't selling

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:46.200
Hard Mountain Dew.
Sugarfoot!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.834
[ Laughter ]
Back in my day,

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.400
if you wanted
a hard Mountain Dew,

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.801
you bought a regular
two-liter Mountain Dew bottle,

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:54.434
poured half out, and filled
the rest up with Everclear.

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.634
It was the only alcohol you had
to be 21 and under to drink.

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.901
Let's just say, after a couple
of hard Mountain Dews,

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:06.200
if you made it back to the
bedroom with your best gal,

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.367
there would be no Baja Blast.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.767
Back in my day,
we weren't banning TikTok.

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:17.767
Back in my day,
if you wanted to get people

00:06:17.767 --> 00:06:19.634
to stop using
a social media platform,

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:22.467
why, you'd just get Elon Musk
to buy it.

00:06:22.467 --> 00:06:24.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.801
Back in my day,
politicians weren't trying

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:28.534
to ban drag shows.

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:30.000
If you didn't want to see men

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.067
in stockings and wigs
and makeup,

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:33.734
well, then you just stayed
the hell away

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.300
from the Founding Fathers.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:38.934
With their big --

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:41.868
[ Cheering ]

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:46.200
They had big old feathers
on their pens.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:50.934
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:53.634
Back in my day, newspapers
weren't dropping "Dilbert"

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:55.834
because its creator went
on a racist rant.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:58.868
Back in my day,
the comics place was an escape,

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:01.767
an innocent place where nothing
controversial ever happened.

00:07:01.767 --> 00:07:04.868
Well, except for that one time
Linus went hard in the paint

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:07.367
and claimed there were
micro magnets in the vaccine.

00:07:07.367 --> 00:07:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:11.467
But, hey, he was right
about the Great Pumpkin.

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:18.133
Back in my day,
we weren't watching

00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:20.901
"The Last of Us" on HBO.
Cable sauce!

00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:22.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.300
Back in my day,
if we were watching HBO,

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.300
it was a little show called
"Real Sex."

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.834
[ Laughter and applause ]
Now, the sex was weird
and everybody was ugly,

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:32.567
but before the Internet,

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:34.834
that was your best option,
if you wanted to see a boob.

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:37.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:37.267 --> 00:07:39.400
You think the "Last of Us" folks
have it bad,

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.801
try cranking it to a group
of 80-year-olds learning

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.367
to have a 30-day orgasm.

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:47.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.601
Come to think about it,
I think that episode

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:49.934
was called "The Blast of Us."

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:52.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.300
I feel like you're purposely
not making eye contact with me.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.267 --> 00:07:59.434
[ Applause ]

00:08:02.234 --> 00:08:04.534
Back in my day,
California wasn't being hit

00:08:04.534 --> 00:08:06.067
with 6.5 feet of snow.

00:08:06.067 --> 00:08:09.334
If you wanted to see 6.5 feet
of white powder in California,

00:08:09.334 --> 00:08:11.200
you had to visit Charlie Sheen

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.767
on the set
of "Two and a Half Men."

00:08:12.767 --> 00:08:13.901
[ Cheering ]
-[ Barks ]

00:08:13.901 --> 00:08:15.033
-Yeah, that's right.

00:08:15.033 --> 00:08:16.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:16.801 --> 00:08:18.200
That's right, I'm winning.

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:22.834
Back in my day, trains full
of toxic chemicals

00:08:22.834 --> 00:08:24.801
weren't constantly derailing
in Ohio.

00:08:24.801 --> 00:08:27.267
Back in my day,
if you wanted to see something

00:08:27.267 --> 00:08:30.834
go off the rails
and cause a toxic environment,

00:08:30.834 --> 00:08:32.701
you had to visit Charlie Sheen
on the set

00:08:32.701 --> 00:08:34.801
of "Two and a Half Men."
-[ Barks ]

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:38.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:39.767
-Diminishing returns, you say?

00:08:39.767 --> 00:08:41.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.968 --> 00:08:46.801
Back in my day,
1,000 British people

00:08:46.801 --> 00:08:48.534
weren't breaking
the Guinness World Record

00:08:48.534 --> 00:08:50.968
for most people
crocheting simultaneously.

00:08:50.968 --> 00:08:53.634
No, If you want to see
that many hookers,

00:08:53.634 --> 00:08:55.601
you had to visit Charlie Sheen
[ Mumbling ]

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:58.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
-[ Growling ]

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.868
-Alright, alright.

00:09:00.868 --> 00:09:01.834
[ Cheering ]
I'll let it go.

00:09:01.834 --> 00:09:04.067
Relax!
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.067 --> 00:09:05.300
It's called the rule of threes.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.667
Twenty-one, for you.

00:09:06.667 --> 00:09:09.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:16.901
Back in my day,
guests at art fairs

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:19.634
weren't breaking Jeff Koons'
balloon animal statues.

00:09:19.634 --> 00:09:20.968
Van Gogh [bleep] yourself!

00:09:20.968 --> 00:09:22.501
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.501 --> 00:09:24.767
Back in my day, if you wanted
to destroy a balloon,

00:09:24.767 --> 00:09:26.734
you had to get
a U.S. fighter jet

00:09:26.734 --> 00:09:28.601
to fire a heat-seeking missile
at it.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:29.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:29.968 --> 00:09:32.100
Why, I still remember
those days,

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.901
way back in February 2023.

00:09:34.901 --> 00:09:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.767
You felt proud
to be an American,

00:09:39.767 --> 00:09:41.801
shooting those balloons
out of the sky.

00:09:41.801 --> 00:09:43.167
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:09:43.167 --> 00:09:45.601
Even though, even now,
you don't really understand

00:09:45.601 --> 00:09:47.000
what was going on.
First, there was just

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.501
the one balloon,
then there were like six,

00:09:48.501 --> 00:09:50.400
then maybe it turned out some
of those weren't real.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.601
There were like multiple
press conferences, I think.

00:09:52.601 --> 00:09:54.534
In any case, it's over now.
Or it's not.

00:09:54.534 --> 00:09:56.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:56.567 --> 00:09:58.000
For as much as we talked
about it,

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.534
I feel like I should know
a few more details.

00:10:00.534 --> 00:10:01.701
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:04.300
News just move so fast,
these days, Rusty.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:06.033
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.033 --> 00:10:07.767
Look. at. me!

00:10:07.767 --> 00:10:10.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:14.434 --> 00:10:16.267
Back in my day,
streaming services

00:10:16.267 --> 00:10:17.534
weren't pulling all their shows.

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:19.000
NBC was.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.434
[ Laughter ]
Did you know we once had a show

00:10:21.434 --> 00:10:23.400
on this network
called "Animal Practice"

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.300
and it starred an actual monkey?
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:27.968
I think it was canceled
mid-episode.

00:10:27.968 --> 00:10:31.267
Meanwhile, I tried to get
an actual dog on this show,

00:10:31.267 --> 00:10:34.934
aka the easiest animal
to get on Earth...

00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:38.434
...and the brass was like,
"How about a stuffed dog

00:10:38.434 --> 00:10:41.367
that's made of a material
you're definitely allergic to?"

00:10:41.367 --> 00:10:42.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
-[ Barks ]

00:10:42.267 --> 00:10:44.100
-No, oh, no.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.067
This was a --
a different thing, Rusty.

00:10:46.067 --> 00:10:47.367
You're a real dog.

00:10:47.367 --> 00:10:49.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:50.934 --> 00:10:53.767
[ Laughter ]

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.901
Back in my day,
Bing didn't have a chat box.

00:10:59.901 --> 00:11:01.367
Well, who knows?
Maybe they did.

00:11:01.367 --> 00:11:02.968
No one ever used it to find out.

00:11:02.968 --> 00:11:04.400
[ Laughter ]

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.868
All I know is that, back then,
if you said the words

00:11:06.868 --> 00:11:09.868
chatbot by Bing,
somebody in a bar might respond

00:11:09.868 --> 00:11:11.133
with a bing bop howdy bow

00:11:11.133 --> 00:11:13.033
[ Laughter ]
and then you'd reply with a

00:11:13.033 --> 00:11:14.501
chitty chitty bebop shoo bop bow

00:11:14.501 --> 00:11:15.701
and then they'd hit you back
with a

00:11:15.701 --> 00:11:17.567
skiddly doo skiddly doo
skiddly doo dop wham

00:11:17.567 --> 00:11:19.467
and then the bartender, he'd
chase you both out with a broom,

00:11:19.467 --> 00:11:21.100
shouting, "I told you
freaky jazz nuts,

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.067
there's no scat singing
in this here establishment.

00:11:23.067 --> 00:11:24.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.501
Go bing your chatty ding dong
somewhere else!"

00:11:26.501 --> 00:11:28.267
[ Laughter ]

00:11:28.267 --> 00:11:30.100
Simpler times.
Well,

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.334
I apologize
that I had to do that,

00:11:32.334 --> 00:11:35.067
but sometimes
this grumpy old Gus has to...

00:11:35.067 --> 00:11:36.501
oh, yeah,
you know what I'm drinking.

00:11:36.501 --> 00:11:38.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:38.701 --> 00:11:39.667
...get his gripe on.

00:11:39.667 --> 00:11:41.300
This has been "Back in My Day."

